,2,null,null,null,0,0,null,"RFR 30","Bronze",null,42],[135726439,"Seminude woman, leaning to the right",1890,0,3,null,4,"8/83/Halbnackte_Frau%2C_nach_rechts_geneigt_%28Auguste_Rodin%29-WUS04125.jpg/330px-Halbnackte_Frau%2C_nach_rechts_geneigt_%28Auguste_Rodin%29-WUS04125.jpg",1,3,1,0,null,null,"Pencil, ink","15.8 × 10 cm",48],[135726466,"Woman Draped in Veils",1890,0,3,null,4,"d/d1/In_Schleier_geh%C3%BCllte_Frau_%28Auguste_Rodin%29-WUS04122.jpg/330px-In_Schleier_geh%C3%BCllte_Frau_%28Auguste_Rodin%29-WUS04122.jpg",1,3,1,0,null,null,"Gouache paint, ink, pencil","17.6 × 8.7 cm",48],[135726884,"Reclining female, seminude, with arms folded behind her head",null,0,3,null,4,"5/5b/Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Femme_allong%C3%A9e%2C_%C3%A0_demi-nue_et_les_bras_repli%C3%A9s_au-dessus_du_visage_-_Mus%C3%A9e_D.4113.jpg/330px-Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Femme_allong%C3%A9e%2C_%C3%A0_demi-nue_et_les_bras_repli%C3%A9s_au-dessus_du_visage_-_Mus%C3%A9e_D.4113.jpg",3,3,1,0,"Femme allongée, à demi-nue et les bras repliés au-dessus du visage","D.04113","Pencil, watercolor paint","24.9 × 32.5 cm",48],[135774243,"Woman in profile in a moment of dancing",1889,0,3,null,4,"e/ec/Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Femme_de_profil_dans_un_mouvement_de_danse_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Rodin_D.8892.JPG/330px-Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Femme_de_profil_dans_un_mouvement_de_danse_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Rodin_D.8892.JPG",1,3,1,0,"Femme de profil dans un mouvement de danse","D.08892","Ink, gouache paint","Height 17.6 cm",48],[135775363,"Woman in profile to the right in a moment of dancing",null,0,3,null,4,"6/6b/Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Femme_dans_un_mouvement_de_danse%2C_de_profil_%C3%A0_droite_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Rodin_D.2190.jpg/330px-Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Femme_dans_un_mouvement_de_danse%2C_de_profil_%C3%A0_droite_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Rodin_D.2190.jpg",1,3,1,0,"Femme dans un mouvement de danse, de profil à droite","D.02190","Pencil, ink","Height 17.6 cm",48],[135777143,"Female nude reclining to the left, one hand to the hip, the other behind the head",null,0,3,null,4,"4/48/Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Femme_nue_allong%C3%A9e_vers_la_gauche%2C_une_main_%C3%A0_la_hanche%2C_l%27autre_derri%C3%A8re_la_t%C3%AAte_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Rodin_D.4132.jpg/330px-Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Femme_nue_allong%C3%A9e_vers_la_gauche%2C_une_main_%C3%A0_la_hanche%2C_l%27autre_derri%C3%A8re_la_t%C3%AAte_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Rodin_D.4132.jpg",1,3,1,0,"Femme nue allongée vers la gauche, une main à la hanche, l'autre derrière la tête","D.04132","Pencil, watercolor paint, wove paper","Height 25.5 cm",48],[135780151,"Female Nude Kneeling, Hands on the back",1900,0,3,null,4,"8/8d/Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Female_Nude_Kneeling%2C_Hands_on_the_back_-_Mus%C3%A9e_RodinD.482.jpg/330px-Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Female_Nude_Kneeling%2C_Hands_on_the_back_-_Mus%C3%A9e_RodinD.482.jpg",1,3,1,0,"Femme nue agenouillée, de face, les mains au dos","D.00482","Pencil, wove paper","Height 31.2 cm",48],[135811327,"Female nude kneeling, bent backwards",1900,0,3,null,4,"1/1d/Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Female_nude_kneeling%2C_bent_backwards_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Rodin_D.1429.jpg/330px-Rodin%2C_Auguste_-_Female_nude_kneeling%2C_bent_backwards_-_Mus%C3%A9e_Rodin_D.1429.jpg",1,3,1,0,"Femme nue agenouillée, de face, mains au dos et tête renversée","D.01429","Pencil, paper","Height 34 cm",48],[136522955,"Figure seen from behind combing his hair",1889,3,7,null,null,null,null,null,0,0,"Figure vue de dos se peignant","Musée Rodin : P.07275","Oil paint",null,27],[139007272,"Portrait de Rodin",1904,10,null,null,3,"5/57/Portrait_de_Rodin%2C_par_Jacques-%C3%89mile_Blanche.jpg/330px-Portrait_de_Rodin%2C_par_Jacques-%C3%89mile_Blanche.jpg",1,33,1,1,null,"P.07270","Oil on canvas","125 × 86.5 cm",53]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaryKind":"excerpt","summaryLicenceUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","factsSource":"Wikidata (CC0)","factsFormat":2,"rankVersion":1,"summaries":{"526178":["The Age of Bronze is a bronze statue by the French sculptor Auguste Rodin (1840–1917). The figure is of a life-size nude male, 72 in.","The Age of Bronze"],"2003287":["The Gates of Hell is a monumental bronze sculptural group work by the French artist Auguste Rodin that depicts a scene from the Inferno, the first section of Dante Alighieri's Divine Comedy. It stands at 6 metres high, 4 metres wide and 1 metre deep (19.7×13.1×3.3 ft) and contains 180 figures.","The Gates of Hell"],"2418237":["The Kiss is an 1882 marble sculpture by the French sculptor Auguste Rodin.","The Kiss (Rodin sculpture)"],"2770535":["Monument to Balzac is a sculpture by Auguste Rodin in memory of the French novelist Honoré de Balzac. According to Rodin, the sculpture aims to portray the writer's persona rather than a physical likeness.","Monument to Balzac"],"3205060":["The Mature Age, also named Destiny, The Path of Life or Fatality (1894–1900) is a sculpture by French artist Camille Claudel. The work was commissioned by the French government in 1895, but the commission was cancelled in 1899 before a bronze was cast.","The Mature Age"],"3205458":["Eternal Springtime is a c. 1884 sculpture by the French artist Auguste Rodin, depicting a pair of lovers. It was created at the same time as The Gates of Hell and originally intended to be part of it.","Eternal Springtime"],"3463880":["Saint John the Baptist (preaching) is a bronze sculpture, by Auguste Rodin.","Saint John the Baptist (Rodin)"],"4792194":["Arles: View from the Wheat Fields was painted by Vincent van Gogh in June 1888, among a number of paintings he made of wheat fields that summer. It is currently displayed at the Musee Rodin in Paris, France.","Arles: View from the Wheat Fields"],"11855751":["Danaid is a sculpture by Auguste Rodin, based on the story of the Danaïdes in Greek myth. It has an alternate name, \"The Spring\".","Danaid (Rodin)"],"13528770":["Portrait of Père Tanguy, painted by Vincent van Gogh in 1887, is one of his three paintings of Julien Tanguy. The three works demonstrate a progression in van Gogh's artistic style after his arrival in Paris.","Portrait of Père Tanguy"],"18003128":["The Thinker, by Auguste Rodin, is a bronze sculpture depicting a nude male figure of heroic size, seated on a large rock, leaning forward, his right elbow placed upon his left thigh, with the back of his right hand supporting his chin in a posture evocative of deep thought and contemplation.","The Thinker"],"19945289":["The Waltz or The Waltzers is a sculpture by the French artist Camille Claudel. It depicts two figures, a man and a woman, locked in an amorous embrace as they dance a waltz.","The Waltz (Claudel)"],"24551519":["I Am Beautiful, also known as The Abduction, is a sculpture of 1882 by the French artist Auguste Rodin, inspired in a fragment from Charles Baudelaire's collection of poems Les Fleurs du mal.","I Am Beautiful (Rodin)"],"24552367":["The Martyr or The Little Martyr is a c.1885 plaster sculpture of a naked dead or sleeping female figure by Auguste Rodin, now in the Musee Rodin.","Flying Figure"],"24568939":["Meditation or The Interior Voice is an 1886 sculpture by Auguste Rodin, showing a young woman resting her head on her right shoulder.","Meditation (Rodin)"],"24569617":["Ugolino and his sons is a plaster sculpture by French artist Auguste Rodin, part of the sculptural group known as The Gates of Hell.","Ugolino and His Sons (Rodin)"],"24943473":["Torso of Adele is an 1878-1884 sculpture by the French artist Auguste Rodin, originally modelled in plaster before being worked in terracotta.","Torso of Adele"],"24943556":["Avarice and Lust is a sculpture by French artist Auguste Rodin, conceived between 1885 and 1887, representing two of the seven capital sins and is part of his sculptural group The Gates of Hell, where it can be found in the lower part of the right door.","Avarice and Lust"],"25415065":["Glaucus is a sculpture by the French artist Auguste Rodin, first conceived in 1886 as a representation of the mythological figure Glaucus, son of Poseidon. Originally made in plaster, bronze casts of it are now in the Brooklyn Museum and the Museo Soumaya.","Glaucus (sculpture)"],"25415087":["The Prodigal Son is a sculpture by Auguste Rodin.","The Prodigal Son (sculpture)"],"26834197":["The Arc of the Covenant or The Cathedral is a sculpture by the French artist Auguste Rodin, conceived in 1908.","The Cathedral (sculpture)"],"31842466":["Sakuntala, also known as Sakountala or Çacountala, is a sculpture by the French artist Camille Claudel, made in several versions in different media from 1886, with a marble version completed in 1905, and bronze castings made from 1905.","Sakuntala (Claudel)"],"67467864":["Adam and Eve, also known as Adam and Eve Sleeping, is a marble sculpture by French sculptor Auguste Rodin, executed in 1905. It is held by the Musée Rodin in Paris.","Adam and Eve (Rodin)"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}